{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Account - User Reported Suspicious Activity",
	"Description": "An end user pressed the \"I don't recognise this\" link in an Okta security notification. This is a first-hand report from the account owner that something they did not do happened, and it deserves triage ahead of most machine-generated signals.\n\nEvent type: user.account.report_suspicious_activity_by_enduser\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_user_reported_suspicious_activity/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/okta_user_reported_suspicious_activity.yml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "0a487185-9b0c-54a9-b545-b09ea701b397",
	"SearchReference": "e1f645ce-5ec1-50d2-8ff8-320f3808f675"
